# ENFORCED (rung 0): the same agent, in a sandbox whose reachable damage is
# enumerable from this file.
#
# Config only. There is no gVisor patch in rung 0 -- if this file needed one, either
# the config approach was not exhausted or we found a real limitation, and the README
# says which.
#
# One argument per line. ${VAR} is expanded by demo.sh.

--runtime=runsc

# gVisor refuses host unix sockets by default (--host-uds=none). host-uds is on
# runsc's overrideAllowlist (runsc/config/flags.go:213), so a container author can ask
# for it per-container without the operator enabling --allow-flag-override. This is
# the one door rung 0 opens deliberately: it is how the agent reaches the broker.
--annotation=dev.gvisor.flag.host-uds=open

# CHANNEL 2, deny-by-default half. An internal docker network whose only other
# occupant is the egress proxy. Every other address is ENETUNREACH from here; the
# allowlist half is enforced by the proxy, outside the sandbox. runsc itself offers no
# host or CIDR filtering (--network takes only sandbox|host|none|plugin), which is the
# negative result rung 2 needs.
--network=ladder-agent
--env=LADDER_PROXY=http://${LADDER_PROXY_IP}:3128

# Identical name resolution to the baseline, so the two columns differ in
# reachability and not in whether a name resolves at all.
--add-host=wiki.corp:169.254.0.10
--add-host=evil.example.com:169.254.0.20

# CHANNEL 3. Read-only root plus exactly two host paths: somewhere to work, and the
# broker socket. Caveat, stated because the demo will show it: /tmp remains writable
# under runsc. It is a sentry-internal tmpfs, so those bytes never reach the host --
# demo.sh proves that rather than asserting it.
--read-only
--volume=${LADDER_RUNTIME_DIR}/scratch:/scratch
--volume=${LADDER_RUNTIME_DIR}/sock:/broker

# CHANNEL 1 is enforced by absence: no credential env vars, no mounted credentials
# file. There is nothing to list here, which is the point.

# Ordinary container hygiene. Not load-bearing for any rung-0 claim, but leaving it
# out would invite the question.
--cap-drop=ALL
--security-opt=no-new-privileges
--user=65534:65534
